<title>CANADA: Gandalf tumbles after disappointing Q4.</title>
<headline>Gandalf tumbles after disappointing Q4.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in networking firm Gandalf Technologies Inc tumbled almost 30 percent early on Thursday after reporting on Wednesday what President Richard Busto called disappointing fourth-quarter results.</p>
<p>Gandalf fell 0.69 to 1.75 in active trading of more than 780,000 shares on the Toronto Stock Exchange. It was down 9/16 to 1-1/4 on Nasdaq.</p>
<p>Ottawa-based Gandalf posted a fourth-quarter loss of US$0.43 a share for the period ended March 31, compared to breakeven a year earlier.</p>
